<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>GrxFirma</displayName>
  <description>GrxFirma computer policies. They are applied in HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\GrxFirma and cannot be changed by non-administrators.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_GrxFirma_0_0_90">GrxFirma 0.0.90 or later</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_GrxFirma_CSC">GrxFirma with CSC remote signing (prototype)</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_GrxFirma_0_0_126">GrxFirma 0.0.126 or later</string>
      <string id="Cat_GrxFirma">GrxFirma</string>
      <string id="Cat_Origenes">Trusted origins</string>
      <string id="Cat_Operacion">Operation</string>
      <string id="Cat_Compatibilidad">Compatibility (lowers security)</string>
      <string id="AllowedDomains">Origins allowed without asking</string>
      <string id="AllowedDomains_Help">Origins (e-government sites) that may request signatures without GrxFirma asking the user whether to trust them. One value per line.

- "sede.example.es" or "*.example.es" allow HTTPS only, on any port.
- "https://sede.example.es:8443", "http://localhost:3000" or "chrome-extension://&lt;id&gt;" allow exactly that scheme, host and port.

If not configured, each new origin is confirmed with the user the first time.</string>
      <string id="DominiosDeConfianza">Additional trusted domains</string>
      <string id="DominiosDeConfianza_Help">Additional trusted domains, with the same syntax as "Origins allowed without asking". One value per line.</string>
      <string id="TSAPermitidas">Timestamp servers (TSA) a request may specify</string>
      <string id="TSAPermitidas_Help">List of timestamp servers (TSA) that a signing request may specify in its tsaURL option. One URL per line; the scheme, host and port are compared, not the path.

For requests from web pages (afirma://, WebSocket and the browser extension), public TSAs are always accepted; the list allows internal-network TSAs as well.

For the local REST service, when this policy is enabled only the TSAs on the list are accepted; with an empty list none is.

Not configured: web pages may specify public TSAs and the REST service any TSA, with a log warning if it is on the internal network. It does not affect the organisation's TSA or the command line.</string>
      <string id="TofuHabilitado">Ask the user about unknown origins</string>
      <string id="TofuHabilitado_Help">Enabled or not configured: when a site that is not on the list requests a signature, GrxFirma asks the user whether to trust it.

Disabled: any origin that is not on the allowed list is rejected without asking. Recommended on managed computers with the full list of sites.</string>
      <string id="ProhibirConfianzaForzada">Prevent users from accepting signatures that show a warning</string>
      <string id="ProhibirConfianzaForzada_Help">When verifying, GrxFirma does not treat a signature as valid if the authority that issued the certificate is not trusted on the computer, if the RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits, if the certificate is a server (component) certificate, if revocation could not be checked, or if the signature uses SHA-1. Users can accept each case on their computer after reading a warning; from then on those signatures show as valid, with a warning that reminds them.

Enabled: users cannot accept any of these cases. GrxFirma does not offer the option and ignores anything already accepted.

Disabled or not configured: users can accept them. If the value cannot be read, it is treated as enabled.</string>
      <string id="WebsocketHabilitado">Resident WebSocket service</string>
      <string id="WebsocketHabilitado_Help">Enabled: GrxFirma keeps a local WebSocket service running in the background for sites that use AutoScript 1.9, even if the site does not launch it.

Disabled or not configured: there is no resident service. Sites can still open, through the afirma:// protocol, a temporary WebSocket channel that closes when each operation ends.</string>
      <string id="WebsocketPermitido">Allow local WebSocket</string>
      <string id="WebsocketPermitido_Help">Enabled or not configured: temporary local WebSocket channels opened through afirma:// are allowed, as is the resident service when separately enabled.

Disabled: all local WebSocket channels are blocked, including temporary afirma:// channels. Sites requiring AutoScript 1.9 over WebSocket will stop working. This policy takes precedence over websocket_habilitado and user settings.</string>
      <string id="RestHabilitado">Local REST service</string>
      <string id="RestHabilitado_Help">Enabled: turns on the local REST service for desktop integrations, which opens a local TCP port.

Disabled or not configured: the REST service is off (default), even if the user tries to enable it in their settings.</string>
      <string id="ManejadorAfirma">Program for signing on websites</string>
      <string id="ManejadorAfirma_Help">Decides which program opens the afirma:// links that public administration websites use to request a signature.

GrxFirma: signatures open in GrxFirma. This is what GrxFirma does without this policy.
AutoFirma: signatures open in AutoFirma, the Spanish Government application. If AutoFirma is not installed on the computer, GrxFirma signs instead.
Ask every time: GrxFirma receives the link and asks which program to sign with.

Enabled: the chosen value takes precedence over the user's choice, and the application setting becomes read-only. The installer also applies it in silent installations.

Disabled or not configured: each user chooses in Settings. If the policy cannot be read, the user's choice is kept and a warning is written to the diagnostic log.

No website can change this setting.</string>
      <string id="NivelLog">Diagnostic log level</string>
      <string id="NivelLog_Help">Level of detail of the diagnostic log. The log never contains documents, keys or passwords, and paths and identifiers are redacted.</string>
      <string id="ManejadorAfirma_GrxFirma">GrxFirma</string>
      <string id="ManejadorAfirma_AutoFirma">AutoFirma</string>
      <string id="ManejadorAfirma_Preguntar">Ask every time</string>
      <string id="NivelLog_Error">Errors only</string>
      <string id="NivelLog_Warn">Warnings</string>
      <string id="NivelLog_Info">Information (recommended)</string>
      <string id="NivelLog_Debug">Debug</string>
      <string id="DirectorioP12">PKCS#12 certificate folder</string>
      <string id="DirectorioP12_Help">Folder from which GrxFirma loads .p12 or .pfx certificate files in addition to the Windows store. It must be a protected local path.</string>
      <string id="TimeoutOperacion">Maximum operation time</string>
      <string id="TimeoutOperacion_Help">Maximum time, in seconds, a signing operation may take before it is cancelled. Default: 30 seconds.</string>
      <string id="MaxTamanoDocumento">Maximum document size</string>
      <string id="MaxTamanoDocumento_Help">Maximum size, in bytes, of a document that can be signed. Default: 52428800 (50 MiB).</string>
      <string id="ProhibirCifradoCMSHeredado">Prohibit CMS envelopes with old ciphers</string>
      <string id="ProhibirCifradoCMSHeredado_Help">Enabling this policy blocks CMS encrypted with legacy ciphers, including AES-CBC. Reading them already requires an explicit user setting, and every permitted use shows a warning. An unreadable policy blocks the exception.</string>
      <string id="PermitirDESLegacy">Allow legacy DES: intermediate server without HTTPS</string>
      <string id="PermitirDESLegacy_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. Without this policy or the user setting, the AutoFirma 1.x DES exchange is blocked even when every server uses HTTPS. Enabling it permits the exchange with a visible warning. Disabling it, or an unreadable policy, blocks the exchange.</string>
      <string id="PermitirSHA1Legacy">Allow SHA-1 signatures</string>
      <string id="PermitirSHA1Legacy_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. Creating SHA-1 signatures is disabled for everyone. Enabling this policy permits the exception with a visible warning. Disabling it also blocks keeping an old SHA-1 signature in an ENI document or co-signature. Historical verification has a separate setting. An unreadable policy blocks the exception.</string>
      <string id="PermitirCMSAESECBLegacy">Allow AutoFirma 1.9 AES-ECB CMS envelopes</string>
      <string id="PermitirCMSAESECBLegacy_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. Allows reading SignedAndEnvelopedData envelopes encrypted with AES in ECB mode created by AutoFirma 1.9.</string>
      <string id="PermitirOrigenVacio">Allow WebSocket without origin</string>
      <string id="PermitirOrigenVacio_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. Allows WebSocket connections without an Origin header or with "Origin: null", which do not identify the connecting site.</string>
      <string id="PermitirRutasDirectas">Allow local paths requested by the site</string>
      <string id="PermitirRutasDirectas_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. Allows a site to specify absolute local paths in load, save and signandsave operations. Without this policy the user always chooses the file.</string>
      <string id="AprobacionAutomaticaNativehost">Sign from the extension without confirmation</string>
      <string id="AprobacionAutomaticaNativehost_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. Allows signing from the browser extension without showing the confirmation dialog. Only for dedicated, controlled workstations.</string>
      <string id="FirmaRemotaCSC">Remote signing with certificates held by a provider (CSC)</string>
      <string id="FirmaRemotaCSC_Help">Signing with certificates held by a trust service provider through the Cloud Signature Consortium API. It is a prototype and has not been tested with real providers.

Enabled: the user can use remote signing from the command line.

Disabled: remote signing cannot be used, even if the user turns it on in their settings.

Not configured: the "firma_remota_csc" setting in the user's config.json decides (off by default).</string>
      <string id="FirmaRemotaCSCOAuth">Remote signing authorisation servers allowed on another host</string>
      <string id="FirmaRemotaCSCOAuth_Help">For security, GrxFirma only accepts a remote signing service that sends authorisation to an OAuth server on the same host and port. If a provider uses a different host, add one line per provider here in the form service=authorisation, for example firma.provider.example=auth.provider.example or firma.provider.example=auth.provider.example:8443. This list replaces the user's list. A malformed line invalidates the list and remote signing is not allowed.</string>
      <string id="FirmaRemotaCSCServicios">Allowed remote signing services</string>
      <string id="FirmaRemotaCSCServicios_Help">Limits remote signing to the providers in this list: one line per service in the form host or host:port (443 if omitted), for example firma.provider.example. GrxFirma does not contact any other service and does not send the PIN or the code anywhere else. A malformed line is ignored and allows no service. Not configured: providers are not limited.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CmsCifradoHeredado">Read CMS with legacy ciphers</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CmsCifradoHeredado_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Leer sobres CMS con cifrados antiguos” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CmsCbc">Read CMS with AES-CBC</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CmsCbc_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Leer sobres CMS con AES-CBC” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CmsRsaV15Crear">Create CMS with legacy RSA key transport</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CmsRsaV15Crear_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Crear CMS con transporte RSA antiguo” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CmsRsaV15Leer">Read CMS with legacy RSA key transport</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CmsRsaV15Leer_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Leer CMS con transporte RSA antiguo” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_AfpAadAmbigua">Open AFP v1 files with ambiguous metadata</string>
      <string id="Permitir_AfpAadAmbigua_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Abrir archivos AFP v1 con metadatos ambiguos” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_AltoClaveFicheroCrear">Create strong protection keys in a file</string>
      <string id="Permitir_AltoClaveFicheroCrear_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Crear claves de protección alta en fichero” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_AltoClaveFicheroLeer">Use strong protection keys stored in a file</string>
      <string id="Permitir_AltoClaveFicheroLeer_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Usar claves de protección alta guardadas en fichero” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CaClaveFichero">Store the local CA key in a file</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CaClaveFichero_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Guardar la clave de la CA local en fichero” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_Sha1Leer">Evaluate old SHA-1 signatures</string>
      <string id="Permitir_Sha1Leer_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Evaluar firmas SHA-1 antiguas” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_XmlC14NAntigua">Evaluate XML with historical canonicalization</string>
      <string id="Permitir_XmlC14NAntigua_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Evaluar XML con canonicalización histórica” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_PdfCifradoHeredado">Sign PDFs with legacy encryption</string>
      <string id="Permitir_PdfCifradoHeredado_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Firmar PDF con cifrado antiguo” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_RsaCorta">Sign with RSA keys under 2048 bits</string>
      <string id="Permitir_RsaCorta_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Firmar con RSA menor de 2048 bits” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_TsaHttp">Contact a timestamp authority over HTTP</string>
      <string id="Permitir_TsaHttp_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Consultar una TSA por HTTP” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_ProxyHttp">Send credentials to an HTTP proxy</string>
      <string id="Permitir_ProxyHttp_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Enviar credenciales a un proxy HTTP” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_TrifasicaHttp">Use three-phase signing over HTTP</string>
      <string id="Permitir_TrifasicaHttp_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Hacer firma trifásica por HTTP” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CaInstalacionAutomatica">Install the local CA automatically</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CaInstalacionAutomatica_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Instalar automáticamente la CA local” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CofirmaSinOriginal">Co-sign or countersign without the original</string>
      <string id="Permitir_CofirmaSinOriginal_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Cofirmar o contrafirmar sin el original” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_LlamanteDesarrollo">Accept a development extension in the native host</string>
      <string id="Permitir_LlamanteDesarrollo_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Aceptar extensión de desarrollo en el host nativo” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
      <string id="Permitir_Pkcs11Experimental">Use experimental PKCS#11 drivers</string>
      <string id="Permitir_Pkcs11Experimental_Help">LOWERS SECURITY. This policy lets the user setting “Usar controladores PKCS#11 experimentales” enable this exception. Disabling the policy blocks it. If unconfigured, the user setting applies; an unreadable policy blocks the exception. Each permitted use shows a warning.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="AllowedDomains"><multiTextBox refId="AllowedDomains_List">Origins (one per line):</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="DominiosDeConfianza"><multiTextBox refId="DominiosDeConfianza_List">Domains (one per line):</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="TSAPermitidas"><multiTextBox refId="TSAPermitidas_List">TSA URLs (one per line):</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="ManejadorAfirma"><dropdownList refId="ManejadorAfirma_Valor" defaultItem="0">Program:</dropdownList></presentation>
      <presentation id="NivelLog"><dropdownList refId="NivelLog_Valor" defaultItem="2">Level:</dropdownList></presentation>
      <presentation id="DirectorioP12"><textBox refId="DirectorioP12_Ruta"><label>Folder:</label></textBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="TimeoutOperacion"><decimalTextBox refId="TimeoutOperacion_Segundos" defaultValue="30">Seconds:</decimalTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="MaxTamanoDocumento"><decimalTextBox refId="MaxTamanoDocumento_Bytes" defaultValue="52428800">Bytes:</decimalTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="FirmaRemotaCSCOAuth"><multiTextBox refId="FirmaRemotaCSCOAuth_List">service=authorisation pairs (one per line):</multiTextBox></presentation>
      <presentation id="FirmaRemotaCSCServicios"><multiTextBox refId="FirmaRemotaCSCServicios_List">Services (one per line):</multiTextBox></presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
